    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0228" n="122" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg122"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCreery to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Valparaiso</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The president, managing director, and one other director of the South American
                    Steamship Company declare before me that the steamer <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Itata</hi> is the property of said company, and that she was taken by force
                    and is now in the service of the revolutionary party without the consent of the
                    company.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. B. McCreery</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
